            "itemId": "pass2rent-car-rental-verifier",
            "slug": "pass2rent-by-odifis",
            "filename": "rp-catalog.json",
            "source": "wordpress",
            "document": {
                "$schema": "https://fides.community/schemas/rp-catalog/v1",
                "orgId": "org:pass2rent-by-odifis",
                "relyingParties": [
                    {
                        "id": "pass2rent-car-rental-verifier",
                        "name": "PASS2RENT - Car rental Verifier",
                        "description": "PASS2RENT Verifier is an in-house OpenID4VP relying party built and operated by Odifis, a Lithuanian SME, for contactless car rental. One unchanged verifier carries the whole rental journey across two EUDI wallets: a privacy-preserving age check at booking (France Identité PID), driver identification at the vehicle (a test mDL from the EU reference wallet), and a fresh, holder- and device-bound mDL presentation at key handover that releases an ephemeral, replay-protected unlock token.\n\nPrivacy is enforced in code, not policy. The rental platform receives a single predicate — age_over_18, with 21/25 thresholds for young-driver pricing — attested directly by the wallet when it serves it (as France Identité does), flagged as derived otherwise. Either way, any birth date disclosed stays at the verification point: read for milliseconds, then stripped before anything is stored or forwarded. No portrait can be stored (no field exists for one); the audit trail is hash-chained and contains zero personal data; claims are encrypted at rest; retention is fail-closed.\n\nTrust is never overstated: the playground PID verifies green against the France Identité IACA trust anchor; an unknown issuer yields an amber \"issuer not recognised\" — never a silent pass. Revocation uses IETF Token Status Lists. Unevaluated checks are labelled, never simulated — including contract signing: advanced electronic signature (AES) in the demo, not yet legal QES.\n\nOpen standards, cross-border by construction: OpenID4VP 1.0 with DCQL, encrypted direct_post.jwt responses, x509_san_dns reader authentication; ISO/IEC 18013-5 mso_mdoc and SD-JWT VC formats. A Lithuanian relying party consuming French national credentials — no bilateral agreement, no national API.\n\nDemo: synthetic identities, real cryptography — not production. Multi-tenant, built so further rental operators can onboard.",
                        "logo": "https://pass2rent.com/logo_pass2rent_web.svg",
                        "website": "https://api.playground.france-identite.gouv.fr/odifis/contactless-rent/en/",
                        "readiness": "use-case-demo",
                        "country": "LT",
                        "interactionMode": "remote",
                        "status": "development",
